  "title": "Why Maternal Healthcare Is Reaching a Breaking Point in Conflict Zones",
  "summary": "For decades, global healthcare initiatives helped make pregnancy and childbirth safer for millions of women. Better access to skilled birth attendants, emergency medical care, vaccinations, and prenatal services significantly reduced maternal deaths across many parts of the world. However, recent humanitarian crises, armed conflicts, and reductions in international aid are threatening to reverse years of progress. Women living in fragile and conflict-affected regions now face increasing risks d",
